1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:03,700
一颗种子。
One seed.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,600
转 137.5°，再长一颗。
Turn 137.5°. Grow another.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,600
就这一条规则，一遍又一遍。
Just this one rule, again and again.

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:28,600
34 条螺旋朝一边，55 条朝另一边。
34 spirals one way, 55 the other.

5
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:34,800
从中心往外数：8、13、21、34、55、89……
Count outward from the centre: 8, 13, 21, 34, 55, 89…

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,600
每个数都是前两个数之和：斐波那契数列。
Each is the sum of the two before it: the Fibonacci sequence.

7
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:46,400
相邻两个数的比，越来越接近 φ。
The ratio of neighbours closes in on φ.

8
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:52,200
用 φ 把一整圈分开，小的那份就是 137.5°。
Split a full turn by φ, and the smaller part is 137.5°.

9
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:57,400
换一个角度试试。
Try a different angle.

10
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:03,800
简单的分数都会重复：种子排成直线，中间留下空隙。
Simple fractions repeat: the seeds line up and leave gaps.

11
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:12,400
φ 是最难被分数逼近的数：它的连分数全是 1。
φ is the number fractions approximate worst: its continued fraction is all ones.

12
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,200
所以黄金角永远不会对齐。
So the golden angle never lines up.

13
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:23,600
每一颗都挤得下，一点空间都不浪费。
Every seed fits, and no space is wasted.

14
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:29,800
同一个角度，长在许多植物上。
The same angle grows in many plants.

15
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:44,400
叶子这样错开，很少正好挡在彼此上方。
Leaves set this way rarely sit right above one another.

16
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:53,600
可是，植物怎么知道 137.5°？
But how does a plant know 137.5°?

17
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:00,400
它不知道。每颗新芽只是长在最有空间的地方。
It doesn't. Each new bud simply grows where there is the most room.

18
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:07,400
就这样，角度自己落到了 137.5° 附近。
And the angle settles near 137.5° by itself.

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,600
自然不会计算。它只是一直在长。
Nature doesn't calculate. It just keeps growing.

20
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:27,200
137.5° · 一个角度
137.5° · One angle
